  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> mixture of hydrogen and helium is contained in a vessel of capacity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0125</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;bar and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The mass of helium in the mixture is .....&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>.</p><p>(Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (Atomic masses of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>, respectively)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PV</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>mix</mo></msub><mi>RT</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>mix</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>083</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Out of total 3 moles Let mole of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>Mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>Then total mass of the mixture will be =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Number of moles of He gas&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p>Mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>moles</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>molar</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mass</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
